# Tailwind CSS v4

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4**, NOT v3. Key differences:

## Configuration

- **No `tailwind.config.ts`**: v4 uses CSS-first configuration via `@theme` blocks in `main.css`
- **No `@apply` in components**: use utility classes directly in templates
- **CSS imports:** `@import "tailwindcss"` + `@import "@nuxt/ui"` in `app/assets/css/main.css`

## Design Tokens (`@theme static` in main.css)

This app follows the **Adjust design system** (v0.3, based on the Adjust Brand
Guidelines 2024). Every brand value lives in `app/assets/css/main.css` — colour
ramps, the type scale, the radii and the font. Never add a new hex, size or
radius to a component; add it there, or reuse what is already defined.

```css
@theme static {
    --font-sans: 'Instrument Sans', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;

    /* type scale — the design system's roles, one per Tailwind step */
    --text-xs: 11.5px;   /* bijschriften        */
    --text-sm: 12.5px;   /* secundaire tekst    */
    --text-base: 13px;   /* lopende tekst       */
    --text-lg: 15px;     /* subkop & paneltitel */
    --text-xl: 20px;     /* kaart- en modaltitel */
    --text-2xl: 24px;    /* sectietitel         */
    --text-3xl: 32px;    /* paginatitel         */

    /* radii — a fixed set of four, never a value in between */
    --radius-sm: 9px;    /* rijen & kleine vlakken */
    --radius-md: 12px;   /* velden & infoblokken   */
    --radius-lg: 16px;   /* kaarten & panelen      */
    /* pill = rounded-full, for buttons and badges  */
}
```

**No shadows on cards.** Surfaces are separated by borders; shadow is reserved
for layers that float (modal, side panel, toast).

## Colors

Colour aliases are configured in `app/app.config.ts` via Nuxt UI and point at
the Adjust ramps defined in `main.css`:

```ts
ui: {
    colors: {
        primary: 'adjust-rood',          // #CF2C28 — primary action & emphasis
        secondary: 'adjust-inkt',        // ink/steel family
        success: 'adjust-succes',        // #1B7F4D
        info: 'adjust-info',             // #2B4155 (Staal)
        warning: 'adjust-waarschuwing',  // #9A6200
        error: 'adjust-rood',            // errors use the same red as the accent
        neutral: 'adjust-inkt',          // text, borders, backgrounds
    },
}
```

**Never hardcode color values**; use the semantic classes: `bg-default`,
`bg-muted`, `bg-elevated`, `bg-accented`, `text-default`, `text-muted`,
`text-dimmed`, `text-highlighted`, `border-default`, `text-primary`.

### Brand rules that override "whatever looks nice"

- **Max one red button per screen.** The rest is secondary or a text link.
- **Text is never red.** Links use Staal with a red underline (`.adj-link`);
  only error messages and microlabels may be red.
- **Dark surfaces (Inkt) are for navigation and orientation, never content.**
- **Green only confirms something that succeeded** — never decoration.
- There is **one theme**. `colorMode` is locked to light in `nuxt.config.ts`;
  do not add a dark variant, it does not exist in the brand.

### Typography roles

Use the `.adj-*` classes from `main.css` for headings and lead text rather than
composing sizes per screen: `.adj-page-title` (one per page), `.adj-section-title`,
`.adj-card-title`, `.adj-subhead`, `.adj-lead`, `.adj-microlabel`, `.adj-link`.

## Responsive Design (Mobile-First)

Always design mobile-first. Base styles = mobile, then add breakpoints:

```
sm:  640px   — large phones, small tablets
md:  768px   — tablets
lg:  1024px  — laptops
xl:  1280px  — desktops
2xl: 1536px  — large desktops
```

### Common patterns:
- `flex-col sm:flex-row`: stack on mobile, row on desktop
- `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`: responsive grid
- `hidden md:block`: hide on mobile, show on desktop
- `w-full max-w-lg mx-auto`: centered container with max width
- `overflow-x-auto`: horizontal scroll for tables on mobile
- `p-4 sm:p-6 lg:p-8`: progressive padding

## Tailwind v4 Breaking Changes from v3

- `@tailwind base/components/utilities` → `@import "tailwindcss"`
- Config is CSS-based (`@theme {}`) not JS-based (`tailwind.config.ts`)
- `cursor-pointer` is no longer default on buttons; we restore it in `main.css`
- Color opacity modifiers work differently: `bg-blue-500/50` (still works)
- Container queries supported natively: `@container`, `@sm`, `@md`

## Do NOT

- Don't create a `tailwind.config.ts` file; use `@theme` in CSS
- Don't use `@apply`; write utility classes in templates
- Don't hardcode colors; use the semantic color system
- Don't use px values for spacing; use Tailwind's spacing scale (4, 6, 8, etc.)
